from the raw certificate `review/mcdsqs80-parent-inputs-v1/mcdsqs80_c21_A.txt` (SHA-256
`49f500c5eedd9a79553e1228d0232e203a749bbda04e3a891c52778dbe9d44a3`): the BLOCKS section and every
`POINT x` section, verbatim.  No symmetry of the certificate is used: every block and every colour
class at every point is checked.

Kernel evaluations (`decide +kernel`; no `native_decide`, no `Lean.ofReduceBool`): `mc_blocks`
(`blockCheck`), `mcPt_0`, ..., `mcPt_79` (`pointCheck` at every point, `Gc80.CertMcPts*`),
`mc79_stsCheck` (`stsColCheck` on the raw `POINT 79` section read on `Fin 79`) and
`mc79_length`.  The semantic conclusions come from the data-independent theorems
`blockCheck_sound`, `pointCheck_sound` (`Gc80.Check80`), `sts_of_check` (`McdKernel.Check`),
`isSQS_of_derived` (`Gc80.Derived`), `colourLowerBound_79` (`Gc80.Counts79`) and `chiPrime_eq_of`
(`McdKernel.Counts`); the target notions are defined in `McdKernel.Target`.
-/

